\begin{abstract}
We concentrate our attention on the qualitative study of the phase portraits of the three-parameter  FitzHugh-Nagumo family and its compactification.  We divide the study into three scenarios
  based on the parameters. One of the scenarios is characterised by the existence of  a Double-zero bifurcation with $\mathbb{Z}_2$--symmetry (singularity of codimension two). 
In this case, we  explicitly exhibit the Pitchfork, Hopf, Belyakov, Double Homoclinic bifurcation/transition curves unfolding the singularity of codimension 2 and plot the bifurcation diagrams. We bridge this analysis with the theory on the associated slow-fast family and  the existence of \emph{canards}. We complete our study with the global compactification of the phase portraits for the family under consideration. 
 This study complements the work summarised in Georgescu, Roc\c soreanu and  Giurgi\c teanu,
{\em Global Bifurcations in FitzHugh-Nagumo Model}, Trends in Mathematics: Bifurcations, Symmetry and Patterns (2003).  \\  \end{abstract}


