\subsection{Description of Figures \ref{bpcn}, \ref{bncn}, \ref{bpcnS}, \ref{bpcpS}, \ref{bpcp} and \ref{bncp} in Appendix \ref{appendix}}
\label{ss:description}
In order to plot the complete phase diagram in the compactified space for the \textbf{Cases A, B} and \textbf{C} in Figures \ref{fig1}, \ref{globalB} and \ref{globalC}, we need to carefully go back through each step of the blow-up procedure, explaining the transformations (blow-ups, directional  transformations and coordinate maps) used at each stage, and clearly stating the resulting system at every step.

Undoing the rescaling \(dt_3=u_6 dt_2\) the phase portrait depicted
in Figures \ref{bpcn}(a), \ref{bncn}(a), \ref{bpcnS}(a), \ref{bpcpS}(a), \ref{bpcp}(a) and \ref{bncp}(a) yields the local phase portrait at the origin of   \eqref{k1}, which is topologically equivalent to that of  Figures \ref{bpcn}(b), \ref{bncn}(b), \ref{bpcnS}(b), \ref{bpcpS}(b), \ref{bpcp}(b) and \ref{bncp}(b), respectively.


Going back through the change of variables \((u_5,v_5)=(u_6, u_6 v_6),\)  the phase portrait depicted
in Figures \ref{bpcn}(b), \ref{bncn}(b), \ref{bpcnS}(b), \ref{bpcpS}(b), \ref{bpcp}(b) and \ref{bncp}(b) yields the local phase portrait at the origin of   \eqref{k2}, which is topologically equivalent to that of Figures \ref{bpcn}(c), \ref{bncn}(c), \ref{bpcnS}(c), \eqref{bpcpS}(c), \ref{bpcp}(c) and \ref{bncp}(c), respectively.

Going back through the change of variables \((u_4,v_4)=(u_5-v_5,v_5),\)  the phase portrait depicted
in Figures \ref{bpcn}(c), \ref{bncn}(c), \ref{bpcnS}(c), \ref{bpcpS}(c), \ref{bpcp}(c) and \ref{bncp}(c),   yields the local phase portrait at the origin of   \eqref{eq4}, which is topologically equivalent to that of Figures \ref{bpcn}(d), \ref{bncn}(d), \ref{bpcnS}(d), \ref{bpcpS}(d), \ref{bpcp}(d) \ref{bncp}(d), respectively.

Going back through the change of variables \((u_3,v_3)=(u_4, 1+v_4)\)  the phase portrait depicted
in Figures \ref{bpcn}(d), \ref{bncn}(d), \ref{bpcnS}(d), \ref{bpcpS}(d), \ref{bpcp}(d) and \ref{bncp}(d) yields the local phase portrait at the origin of system \eqref{eq3}, which is topologically equivalent to that of Figures \ref{bpcn}(e), \ref{bncn}(e), \ref{bpcnS}(e), \ref{bpcpS}(e), \ref{bpcp}(e) and \ref{bncp}(e), respectively.

Undoing the rescaling \(dt_2=u_3 dt_1\) the phase portrait depicted
in Figures \ref{bpcn}(e), \ref{bncn}(e), \ref{bpcnS}(e), \ref{bpcpS}(e), \ref{bpcp}(e) and \ref{bncp}(e) yields the local phase portrait at the origin of   \eqref{k4}, which is topologically equivalent to that of Figures \ref{bpcn}(f) and \ref{bncn}(f), \ref{bpcnS}(f), \ref{bpcpS}(f), \ref{bpcp}(f) and \ref{bncp}(f),  respectively.

Going back through the change of variables \((u_2,v_2)\rightarrow (u_3,v_3/u_3),\) the phase portrait depicted in Figures \ref{bpcn}(f), \ref{bncn}(f), \ref{bpcnS}(f), \ref{bpcpS}(f), \ref{bpcp}(f) and \ref{bncp}(f), yields the local phase portrait at the origin of system \ref{k5}, which is topologically equivalent to that of Figures \ref{bpcn}(g), \ref{bncn}(g), \ref{bpcnS}(g), \ref{bpcpS}(g), \ref{bpcp}(g) and \ref{bncp}(g),  respectively.

Going back through the change of variables \((u_1,v_1)=(u_2-v_2, v_2),\) the phase portrait depicted in Figures \ref{bpcn}(g), \ref{bncn}(g), \ref{bpcnS}(g), \ref{bpcpS}(g), \ref{bpcp}(g) and \ref{bncp}(g) yields the local phase portrait at the origin of   \eqref{k6}, which is topologically equivalent to that of Figures  \ref{bpcn}(h), \ref{bncn}(h), \ref{bpcnS}(h), \ref{bpcpS}(h), \ref{bpcp}(h) and \ref{bncp}(h), respectively.

Undoing the rescaling \(dt_1=u_1 dt\) the phase portrait depicted in Figures \ref{bpcn}(h), \ref{bncn}(h), \ref{bpcnS}(h), \ref{bpcpS}(h), \ref{bpcp}(h) and \ref{bncp}(h) yields the local phase portrait at the origin of   \eqref{k7}, which is topologically equivalent to that of Figures \ref{bpcn}(i), \ref{bncn}(i), \ref{bpcnS}(i), \ref{bpcpS}(i), \ref{bpcp}(i) and \ref{bncp}(i),  respectively.

Going back through the change of variables \((u,v)\rightarrow (u_1,v_1/u_1),\) the phase portrait depicted in Figures \ref{bpcn}(i), \ref{bncn}(i), \ref{bpcnS}(i), \ref{bpcpS}(i), \ref{bpcp}(i) and \ref{bncp}(i) yields the local phase portrait at the origin of   \eqref{k8}, which is topologically equivalent to that of Figures \ref{bpcn}(j), \ref{bncn}(j), \ref{bpcnS}(j), \ref{bpcpS}(j), \ref{bpcp}(j) and \ref{bncp}(j), respectively.

This allows us to plot the complete phase diagram in the compactified space for the \textbf{Cases A, B} and \textbf{C} in Figures \ref{fig1}, \ref{globalB} and \ref{globalC}. The local phase portraits of the blow-down at the origin of the different local charts have been plotted in Figures \ref{bpcn}--\ref{bncp}.

