\caption{Relationship between OT height and sun elevation angle in the database. Black dots represent detected OTs, with shadow-based height estimates. The red, purple, and blue lines correspond to theoretical OT height estimates based on different shadow lengths (4 km, 2 km, and 1 km, respectively). The shaded regions indicate potential improvements in OT detection due to improved spatial resolution achievable with the upcoming MTG satellite mission. The three unique symbols on the right mark the maximum sun elevation angles at various locations (Rome, Prague, and Copenhagen).}
