\section{The age of a DESI universe is $\mathbf{13.7 \pm 0.07}$ Gyr}
\label{Two ages for the universe}


\par
In $\Lambda$CDM cosmology,
the age of the universe 
is~\cite{Weinberg2010p34-45, CahillCUP2ageofuniverse}.
\begin{equation}
t_{\Lambda\text{CDM}}(1) ={}  \frac{1}{H_0} \int_0^1
\!\! \frac{da}{ \sqrt{\Omega_{\Lambda} \, a^2
+ \Omega_{k}   
+ \Omega_{m} \, a^{-1}  
+ \Omega_{r} \, a^{-2} } }  
= 13.8 \,\,\text{Gyr} .
\label {LCDM time}
\end{equation}

\par

In DESI cosmology,
the Pantheon+, Union3 
and DESY5 universes are younger 
by 51, 191, and 119 Myr respectively:
\begin{align}
t_{\text{P+}}(1) ={}  \frac{1}{H_0} 
\! \int_0^1
\!\! \frac{da}
{ \sqrt{\Omega_{\Lambda} \, a^{3.374} \,
