\section{Pseudo $H$-type nilmanifold ${N}_{3,4}$}\label{sec.N3.4}


It is known that  the Clifford algebra $\operatorname{Cl}(\mathbb{R}^{3,4})$ has two non-equivalent minimal admissible $8$-dimensional modules.
Moreover, the corresponding $15$-dimensional pseudo $H$-type Lie algebras are isomorphic and isometric, see~\cite[Theorem 12]{FuMa17}.
Therefore, it sufficient to check only one such pseudo $H$-type nilmanifold $N_{3,4}$.

The pseudo $H$-type nilmanifold $N_{3,4}$ has dimension $15$,
and the corresponding left invariant metric is generated by
