\subsubsection{Constructing measures from norm relations}\label{sec:horconstr}Suppose we are given a sequence of elements 
$$\theta_n \in R\left[\prod_{i = 1}^nG_i\right],$$
$n \in \N$, such that we have the following ``norm relation'': the image of $\theta_n$ under the natural projection 
$$\pi_n : R\left[\prod_{i = 1}^nG_i\right] \rightarrow R\left[\prod_{i = 1}^{n-1}G_i\right]$$
is of the form $\alpha_n \cdot \theta_{n-1}$
for some $\alpha_n \in R\left[\prod_{i = 1}^{n-1}G_i\right]$ for every $n \ge 1$. Suppose that $\alpha_n \in R\left[\prod_{i=1}^nG_i\right]^{\times}$ for every $n \ge 1$. Note that for any $m \le n$, we have a canonical section of $\pi_n$
\begin{equation}\label{eq:canonicalsection}i_n : \prod_{i = 1}^mG_i \rightarrow \prod_{i = 1}^nG_i, \hspace{1cm} x \mapsto (x,e_{m+1},\ldots,e_n)\end{equation}
where $e_i \in G_i$ is the identity element of the group $G_i$. We suppress the dependence of $i_n$ on $m$ since it is clear that the $i_n$'s are compatible for all $m \le n$. 
 Then we have a sequence
$$\nu_n := \frac{\theta_n}{\prod_{j = 1}^ni_n(\alpha_j)} \in R\left[\prod_{i = 1}^nG_i\right]$$
which are compatible under the natural projections $\pi_n : R[\prod_{i = 1}^nG_i] \rightarrow R[\prod_{i = 1}^{n-1} G_i]$. To see this compatibility, note that $\pi_n(i_n(\alpha)) = i_{n-1}(\alpha)$ for any $\alpha \in R[\prod_{i = 1}^mG_i]$, $m < n$. Hence
\begin{align*}\pi_n(\nu_n) = \pi_n\left(\frac{\theta_n}{\prod_{j = 1}^ni_n(\alpha_j)}\right) 
&= \frac{\pi_n(\theta_n)}{\prod_{j = 1}^n\pi_n(i_n(\alpha_j))} = \frac{\alpha_n \cdot \theta_{n-1}}{\alpha_n \cdot \prod_{j=1}^{n-1}i_{n-1}(\alpha_j)} \\
&= \frac{\theta_n}{\prod_{j=1}^{n-1}i_{n-1}(\alpha_j)} = \nu_{n-1}.
\end{align*}
Thus we get an element 
$$\nu = \varprojlim_{\pi_n} \nu_n \in \Lambda_R^{\mathrm{hor}}.$$
