\begin{equation}\label{eq:chir}v_p(\nu(\chi_1)) \leq \frac{1}{p-1}.\end{equation}
If furthermore $p > 2$ holds then for any character $\chi : \prod_{n \in \N \setminus\{1\}}G_n \rightarrow \C_p^{\times}$ there exists $\sigma \in \mathrm{Gal}(\Q(\mu_p)/Q)$ such that
\begin{equation}\label{eq:chirchi}v_p(\nu(\chi_1\chi^{\sigma}))\leq \frac{1}{p-1}.\end{equation}
%In particular, in this case we can pick $e=\tfrac{r}{p-1}$ and $I\subset \{1,\ldots, r\}$ in Corollary \ref{cor:nonvanishingPS}.%viewed as aone can pick $I=\{1\}$ in Theorem 
