$$p\nu_{\chi_1,1} = \nu_{\chi_1}(\mathbf{1}) + \sum_{\chi \in \widehat{G}\setminus \{1\}}\nu_{\chi_1}(\chi) = \nu(\chi_1) + \sum_{\chi \in \widehat{G} \setminus \{1\}}\nu(\chi_1\chi)$$
where $\widehat{G}$ denotes the dual group of $G$ and $\mathbr{1}$ denotes the trivial character. Taking $v_p$ of this equation we thus get
$$1 \le v_p(p\nu_{\chi_1,1}) = v_p\left(\nu(\chi_1) + \sum_{\chi \in \widehat{G} \setminus \{1\}}\nu(\chi_1\chi)\right).$$
