\begin{definition}\label{ex-defi}
    An oriented graph $G$ of $n$ vertices is \emph{$\eta$-extremal} if there are $3$ or $4$ disjoint vertex subsets $A,B,C,D \subset V(G)$ (here $A$ or $C$ can be empty) satisfying that:
     \begin{itemize}
        \item $|A| + |C| = (1/2 \pm O(\eta)) n$,
        \item $|B| = (1/4 \pm O(\eta)) n$,
        \item $|D| = (1/4 \pm O(\eta)) n$;
    \end{itemize}
    and the edges satisfying that:


