\begin{abstract}
 %The specification curve literature brings integrity into the scientific record, but further work remains to be done to adequately integrate researcher-based degrees of freedom.
We present \texttt{RobustiPy}, a next generation Python‐based framework for model‐uncertainty quantification and multiverse analysis, released under the GNU GPL v3.0. Through the integration of efficient bootstrap-based confidence intervals, combinatorial exploration of dependent‐variable specifications, model selection and averaging, and two complementary joint‐inference routines, \texttt{RobustiPy} transcends existing uncertainty‐quantification tools. Its design further supports rigorous out-of-sample evaluation and apportions the predictive contribution of each covariate. We deploy the library across five carefully constructed simulations and ten empirically grounded case studies drawn from high-impact literature and teaching examples, including a novel re-analysis of `unexplained discrepancies' in famous prior work. To illustrate its performance, we time-profile \texttt{RobustiPy} over roughly 672 million simulated linear regressions. These applications showcase how \texttt{RobustiPy} not only accelerates robust inference but also deepens our interpretive insight into model sensitivity across the vast analytical multiverse within which scientists operate.
\end{abstract} \vspace{.05in}

