The operators are constructed using smeared links. Specifically, we apply APE~\cite{Albanese:1987ds,Morningstar:2003gk} smearing to spatial links, while temporal links are smeared using the multihit technique~\cite{Huntley:1985ts,Bicudo:2018jbb}.



We use linear combinations of the staples shown in Fig. \ref{fig:sub-operators} consisting of rotations around the principal axis and reflections over the two parity planes to compute the Wilson correlation matrix for each irreducible representation of the flux-tube. 






